<%# Faithful port of the legacy SPA `Hujah.jsx` flag modal (a Bootstrap Modal +
    ListGroup, 3 reasons: spam / abusive / irrelevant). Native <dialog> driven by the
    shared `dialog` controller. Each reason is a submit button that posts its subject
    straight to POST /hoojah/:slug/flags — no client-side reason state needed, and the
    menu still works with JS off (the form submits, the server redirects).

    Locals: hujah. The `flag_control` wrapper is the Turbo-Stream replace target
    (create.turbo_stream.erb swaps it for a confirmation).

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.8) —
    docs/design-system/components/overlays/Dialog.prompt.md. The panel itself was already
    the design system's dialog to the letter — 8px rounding, the large shadow, the 40%
    black backdrop, 448px max width, a hairline header carrying the title and an X — so
    the shell does not move, and neither does the header — the same markup
    `users/_profile_edit` carries. Dialog.prompt.md names all three of these ("Flag this
    hoojah, Challenge @user to a debate, Edit your profile") as one component, and their
    headers really are one shape: the X in all three now comes from
    `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey")`. That was true again only after a
    follow-up: Task 4.8 moved this X and the challenge dialog's onto the helper and left
    `users/_profile_edit` on the hand-typed string it kept in Task 4.6, so for one commit
    two of the three headers were on the helper and one was not. A hand-typed class on any
    of the three is a divergence to close, not a local style. What changed:

    - The trigger is a row inside `hujahs/show`'s "More actions" menu, so it is a
      DropdownMenu MenuItem and now says so via `ds_menu_item_classes`. Its two
      Bootstrap-era class names were dead — no rule for either exists anywhere in the
      bundle, exactly as Task 4.6 found on the profile-edit pencil — so they are replaced
      by what they were pretending to be. Coming from the helper buys three things the
      hand-typed string was missing: 14px UI text, the 4px rounding, and the menu-row
      hover fill DropdownMenu.prompt.md specifies. The type size in particular closes a
      real seam: `flags/create.turbo_stream.erb` replaces this row with a confirmation
      that is already 14px, so flagging used to swap a 16px row for a 14px one. The
      tone is the same `neutral` pink the signed-out "Login to flag this hoojah" row
      beside it already takes ("destructive/report rows take tone=neutral"), and the
      display override is the ONE override that call site may make — see the note on
      MENU_ITEM_BASE. The pointer cursor has to be asked for: Tailwind v4 no longer
      gives a button one.
    - The reason list loses the 1px edge and the rounding that boxed it in. That is the
      same correction Task 4.7 made to the two analytics surfaces, and the authority is
      readme.md's VISUAL FOUNDATIONS assigning the greys by job: "Tailwind grays for
      hairlines (`#f3f4f6`), field borders/tracks (`#e5e7eb`), hover fills (`#f9fafb`)".
      `#f3f4f6` is the HAIRLINE token — what `ui/_divider` spends INSIDE a surface — so a
      `border` in it drawn around the outside of one is off-token, and the rounding was
      only there to soften a box that should not have been drawn. NOT because "rounding is
      forbidden": Card.prompt.md's rule is the narrow "Never round a feed card", and this
      design system rounds plenty else — readme.md gives dialogs `rounded-lg` and menus
      `rounded`, and `--radius: 4px` exists for small chrome. The `<dialog>` this list
      sits inside is itself `rounded-lg`. It does NOT become a
      `ui/_card` the way those two did — a card nested in a dialog is the second shadow
      the same rule rejects — so what is left is what the box was already expressing:
      three rows separated by the shared hairline, hovering to the grey the prompt file
      names. Row padding is untouched, so the rows sit exactly where they sat.
    - The X and Cancel go through `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey")` —
      bare, borderless, transparent, grey, no font size of its own. That is Dialog.prompt.md's
      "bare grey Cancel" and the variant the notification rows already use. Cancel drops
      its hand-typed padding because the variant is padding-free and passing both would be
      a same-family coin flip; it therefore lines up with the body copy above it instead
      of sitting 16px further in. Both controls gain the pointer cursor and the house
      press state.

    FROZEN: `dom_id(hujah, :flag_control)`, the wrapper `create.turbo_stream.erb`
    replaces, and `dom_id(hujah, :flag_dialog)`, which the same template closes remotely;
    every `data-*` on the wrapper, the trigger and the dialog; the POST to
    /hoojah/:slug/flags and the three `flag[subject]` values; and every word of copy —
    spec/system/flag_spec.rb clicks "Flag this hoojah" and "It's suspicious or spam" by
    name. %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(hujah, :flag_control) %>" data-controller="dialog">
  <button type="button" data-action="dialog#open"
          class="<%= ds_menu_item_classes(tone: "neutral") %> flex items-center gap-1 cursor-pointer">
    <%= lucide_icon("flag", class: "w-4 h-4") %> Flag this hoojah
  </button>

  <dialog id="<%= dom_id(hujah, :flag_dialog) %>"
          data-dialog-target="dialog"
          data-action="click->dialog#backdropClose close->dialog#restoreFocus"
          aria-labelledby="dialog-title-flag"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-lg p-0 w-full max-w-md backdrop:bg-black/40">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-100">
      <h5 id="dialog-title-flag" class="text-lg font-medium m-0">Flag this hoojah</h5>
      <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close" aria-label="Close"
              class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">
        <%= lucide_icon("x", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
      </button>
    </div>

    <%= form_with url: hujah_flags_path(hujah.slug), method: :post, class: "p-4" do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-grey mb-3">Why are you flagging this hoojah?</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <button type="submit" name="flag[subject]" value="spam"
                class="text-left px-4 py-3 hover:bg-gray-50 border-0 bg-card cursor-pointer">
          It's suspicious or spam
        </button>
        <%= render "ui/divider" %>
        <button type="submit" name="flag[subject]" value="abusive"
                class="text-left px-4 py-3 hover:bg-gray-50 border-0 bg-card cursor-pointer">
          It's abusive or harmful
        </button>
        <%= render "ui/divider" %>
        <button type="submit" name="flag[subject]" value="irrelevant"
                class="text-left px-4 py-3 hover:bg-gray-50 border-0 bg-card cursor-pointer">
          It's irrelevant to the parent hoojah
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="text-right mt-4">
        <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close"
                class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">Cancel</button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dialog>
</div>
